{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nU \\longmapsto\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U)}(\n\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}, \\mathcal{G}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U})\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$\\SheafHom(\\mathcal{F},\\mathcal{G})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-section-internal-hom}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0a4ebb992ab43db3cb14ffc5b987e7e509c08388b530aba270d5d8fd2296b2e4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:200dacb01992aa487ed2ffdebc9d08ab21f140789b6ce71c2695f5f6d8e0f27f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe previous lemma implies that given two sheaves <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002> on a site <MATH_0003> the rule\n<MATH_0004>\ndefines a sheaf <MATH_0005>.\nThis is a kind of <TEXTITOPEN_0001>internal hom sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>. It is\nseldom used in the setting of sheaves of sets, and more usually\nin the setting of sheaves of modules, see\nModules on Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8285d0868994c056819f3df21a86b7eeb0b9980bf2cb471c43bde4366ed6ce90", "unit_id": "tag:04TP:prose-0002"}
