{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "\\begin{align*}\n\\Mor(\\mathcal{G}, j_*(\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}))\n& =\n\\Mor(\\mathcal{G}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}, \\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}) \\\\\n& =\n\\Mor(j_!(\\mathcal{G}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}), \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& =\n\\Mor(\\mathcal{G} \\times h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& =\n\\Mor(\\mathcal{G}, \\SheafHom(h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F}))\n\\end{align*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-internal-hom-sheaf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-compute-j-shriek-restrict}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:315e634fc2954c07be038f54a7161cb3e2b553703d95e251dd79ad4a3b8bc21f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f6d80f4a6872d14d74fce238be92089143e5c85618e87599327c1b6aa80e0e00", "source_text": "This can be shown by directly constructing an isomorphism\nof sheaves. Instead we argue as follows.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a sheaf on <MATH_0002>.\nThen\n<MATH_0003>\nand we conclude by the Yoneda lemma. Here we used\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f8ff1eda26d25943d9e84beca00aae0c5a233bff864a91a6e37ae1a89dbc895", "unit_id": "tag:0D7X:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}/U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$i, j \\in I$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\varphi_{ij} :\n\\mathcal{F}_i|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}_j|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$i, j, k \\in I$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}_i|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j \\times_U U_k}\n\\ar[rr]_{\\varphi_{ik}}\n\\ar[rd]_{\\varphi_{ij}} & &\n\\mathcal{F}_k|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j \\times_U U_k} \\\\\n&\n\\mathcal{F}_j|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j \\times_U U_k}\n\\ar[ru]_{\\varphi_{jk}}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5fdd9449b6d20f459dfe08df6d95fefe4f6a5dee9188b7ab9cffba56b720d8d1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a8b795c6e38c1f9b5d0e4205f2a1f08bba859aba024c74053f288877385bb80", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a covering of <MATH_0003>.\nFor each <MATH_0004> let <MATH_0005> be a sheaf of sets on\n<MATH_0006>.\nFor each pair <MATH_0007>, let\n<MATH_0008>\nbe an isomorphism of sheaves of sets. Assume in addition\nthat for every triple of indices <MATH_0009> the\nfollowing diagram is commutative\n<MATH_0010>\nWe will call such a collection of data\n<MATH_0011>\na <TEXTITOPEN_0001>glueing data for sheaves of sets with respect to\nthe covering <MATH_0012><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:140c0b778303f9d22a190c68226614f44fd17da3