{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\varphi_i : \\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i} \\to \\mathcal{F}_i\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n\\ar[d]_{\\text{id}} \\ar[r]_{\\varphi_i} &\n\\mathcal{F}_i|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j} \\ar[d]^{\\varphi_{ij}} \\\\\n\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j} \\ar[r]^{\\varphi_j} &\n\\mathcal{F}_j|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-glue-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c8fa6034b5f34840b693c4e548c7c07d5d6b08e5b20400a67903354ce96ac416", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5e5c29985774a12b747c283317b8e59e6689b38661cfa7243646582cb8e67071", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a covering of <MATH_0003>.\nGiven any glueing data <MATH_0004>\nfor sheaves of sets with respect to the covering <MATH_0005>\nthere exists a sheaf of sets <MATH_0006> on <MATH_0007>\ntogether with isomorphisms\n<MATH_0008>\nsuch that the diagrams\n<MATH_0009>\nare commutative.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8ba1f893fe1a73a6b9c27ad11abc7412f52ef2712558d97c0388fcb7c515e27d", "unit_id": "tag:04TR:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0003": "$a : V \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}(V/U) = \\{\n(s_i)_{i \\in I} \\in \\prod_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i(U_i \\times_U V/U_i)\n\\mid\n\\varphi_{ij}(s_i|_{U_i \\times_U U_j \\times_U V})\n=\ns_j|_{U_i \\times_U U_j \\times_U V}\n\\}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:65619da581a96939d54acf1a4e2aa00306aeac63bdf1ab8b8d50a9af09f7c975", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf097afcdcbc2ee0e03f15467bde44101cf669ae692d8371f9c8119c86bc5f29", "source_text": "Let us describe how to construct the sheaf <MATH_0001> on\n<MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003> be an object of <MATH_0004>.\nThen\n<MATH_0005>\nWe omit the construction of the restriction mappings.\nWe omit the verification that this is a sheaf.\nWe omit the construction of the isomorphisms <MATH_0006>,\nand we omit proving the commutativity of the diagrams\nof the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3fbf967f5de845c908753b708e98678033e68e75b7e0b1d625e1fa094cf72ade", "unit_id": "tag:04TR:proof"}
